  "answer": {
    "question": "Why are adults waiting nine weeks for a seat?",
    "text": "The sources don't say why adults wait nine weeks; they only report that 287 adults were on the waitlist at year end and that the average wait was nine weeks [1].\nMost adults on the waitlist were at the Eastgate and Riverside sites [1]. Demand also grew. Harborlight enrolled 1,148 adult learners in FY2026, up from 936 the year before [2]. But the report never ties that growth to the wait.\nStaff want to add a sixth site at the Eastgate branch library, plus two site coordinators. They estimate it would serve 180 more learners a year and cut the waitlist in half [3]. The sources don't name a cause, such as too few tutors, staff or rooms.",
    "lead": "The sources don't say why adults wait nine weeks; they only report that 287 adults were on the waitlist at year end and that the average wait was nine weeks [1].",
